From: pyra-backlight <pyra-backlight@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: pyra v5.3: make the keyboard light an LED

The keyboard light is a pwm-backlight, so /sys/class/backlight holds both
the panel and the keyboard, and desktop software that picks "the"
backlight by taking the first entry drives the keyboard. Declare it as a
pwm-leds LED named pyra::kbd_backlight instead, the convention UPower and
systemd-backlight look for. Same PWM, period and pins.

Only the Pyra V5.3 board file changes; pyra-mainboard-common.dtsi keeps
the backlight node for the other board revisions.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5-letux-cortex15-v5.3+pyra-v5.3.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/omap5-letux-cortex15-v5.3+pyra-v5.3.dts
@@ -68,3 +68,37 @@
 	status = "okay";
 	memory-region = <&dsp_memory_region>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * The keyboard light as an LED rather than a second backlight.
+ *
+ * pyra-mainboard-common.dtsi declares it as a pwm-backlight, which puts
+ * keyboard-backlight next to the panel in /sys/class/backlight. Desktop
+ * software treats that class as "the screen" and takes the first entry
+ * when it cannot tell which is which; MATE takes the keyboard. The
+ * convention for keyboard lights is an LED named *::kbd_backlight, which
+ * UPower and systemd-backlight both look for by that name.
+ *
+ * Same PWM, period (8.3 kHz) and pins as the backlight node. max-brightness
+ * is 100 so that brightness is the duty cycle in percent, the scale of the
+ * old brightness-levels table (0 1 2 5 10 20 40 60 100); pwm-leds is
+ * linear, so userspace that wants those nine steps steps through them
+ * itself. pwm-leds in 5.6 has no default brightness, so the light starts
+ * off rather than at the old 5% until systemd-backlight restores the saved
+ * level.
+ */
+/ {
+	/delete-node/ keyboard-backlight;
+
+	keyboard-leds {
+		compatible = "pwm-leds";
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
+		pinctrl-0 = <&pyra_keyboard_backlight_pins>;
+
+		keyboard {
+			label = "pyra::kbd_backlight";
+			pwms = <&pwm8 0 120000 0>;
+			max-brightness = <100>;
+		};
+	};
+};
